xt gets created from the current {@link DocumentParserContext} and returned, indicating\n+     * that the source for the sub-context has been captured, to avoid double-storing parts of its contents to ignored source.\n+     */\n+    public final DocumentParserContext addIgnoredFieldFromContext(IgnoredSourceFieldMapper.NameValue ignoredFieldWithNoSource)\n+        throws IOException {\n+        if (canAddIgnoredField()) {\n+            if (parentArrayField !\u003d null\n+                \u0026\u0026 parent !\u003d null\n+                \u0026\u0026 parentArrayField.equals(parent.fullPath())","submitted_line":320},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The addition of `ignoredFieldsMissingValues` and `parentArrayField` to `DocumentParserContext` seems appropriate for handling missing values and nested arrays. However, the introduction of `parentArrayField` might lead to confusion as it is not clear how it interacts with other fields like `parent`. Ensure that this field is correctly managed and does not introduce unintended side effects.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParserContext.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParserContext.java-5483:5495,6269:6281,6284:6296-5217:5283,5293:5316,5826:5840,6100:6160,6169:6210,6733:6747,6750:6764","promptId":"#9C4PE","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParserContext.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParserContext.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":5483,"endPos":5495,"startLine":149,"startLineOffset":16,"endLine":149,"endLineOffset":28,"length":13},{"pos":6269,"endPos":6281,"startLine":168,"startLineOffset":13,"endLine":168,"endLineOffset":25,"length":13},{"pos":6284,"endPos":6296,"startLine":168,"startLineOffset":28,"endLine":168,"endLineOffset":40,"length":13}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":5217,"endPos":5283,"startLine":143,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":143,"endLineOffset":74,"length":67},{"pos"